.TH MINE-CLASSIC 6 2026-11-26 "minesweeper-cli 0.2.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
mine-classic, mine-path \- minesweeper games for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mine-classic
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mine-path
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Two minesweeper games that run in a text terminal.
.PP
.B mine-classic
is the classic game: open every square that does not hide a mine.
The first dig is always safe, and digging a number whose flags are all
placed opens its remaining neighbours.
.PP
.B mine-path
is the pathfinder game: walk from the top left corner to the goal
.RB ( G )
in the bottom right corner, learning only about the squares you step on.
Every board has a safe route.
The score is a penalty time, and lower is better: the seconds taken plus
30 seconds for every safe square left unexplored and for every mark
placed on a safe square.
Marking mines is optional.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Play the board with seed
.IR N .
The seed is shown during play, and the same seed gives the same board on
every platform.
Scores are not saved.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Monochrome output.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Use only ASCII characters on the board.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run the built-in checks and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.SH KEYS
.SS mine-classic
.TP 16
Arrows, WASD, HJKL
Move the cursor.
.TP
Space, Enter
Dig.
.TP
F
Place or remove a flag.
.TP
M, ?
Place or remove a question mark.
.TP
P
Pause; the board is hidden.
.TP
Q
Quit the game.
.SS mine-path
.TP 16
Arrows, WASD, HJKL
Move.
.TP
Q E Z C, Y U B N
Move diagonally.
.TP
M or F, then a direction
Mark or unmark a suspected mine next to you.
.TP
P
Pause; the board is hidden.
.TP
Shift+Q
Quit the game.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, output is monochrome.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base folder for the score files, if set to an absolute path.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to find the score folder when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mine\-cli/
One score file per game and difficulty, such as
.I classic\-beginner.txt
or
.IR path\-hp48.txt ,
each holding the top 5 scores with the date and time of each win.
.SH AUTHORS
German Pulido.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/gapf2010/minesweeper-cli
